    "lawCode": "Amd §§483-h, 17 & 429, Soc Serv L; amd §201, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6031\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the social services law and the public\nhealth law, in relation to home visiting programs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to require an online resource to enhance\naccess to information regarding New York State's home visiting programs.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1-4 amend certain sections of the social services law and the\npublic health law to require the office of children and family services\nand the department of health to make available home visiting program\ninformation to the council on children and families for an internet\nmapping resource. Such internet mapping resource would include the\nfollowing information: program name, program address and phone number,\nand program recipient eligibility criteria.\n\nSection 5 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent information regarding home visiting programs is scattered and\ninfrequently updated. Including information about home visiting programs\non the Council on Children and Families internet mapping resource would\nensure regular updates and that more comprehensive information is\nincluded, improving accessibility of home visiting services for eligible\nfamilies. In addition, the bill would ensure that the mapping resource\nwould be available online to the public on a permanent basis.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the 90th day after it shall have become a\nlaw.\n",
